files: The generated files

Each package is written to a folder named by its import path: pkg.hpp (everything other
packages and its own units need), one translation unit for each .gp file that has functions
(render.gp.cpp), pkg_desc.cpp (the descriptors of its types) and pkg_init.cpp (package
variables, gp_var_init, gp_init_funcs; main's also gp_init_all and main). gocpp emit prints
all the files, each after a line //// gpkg/<import path>/<file>, packages in import order.

The folder is the same in every build of a program, so #line paths and the object cache are
stable: a unit that did not change, and whose headers did not, is not compiled again. A
declaration in a header has no #line, so a change in a function body does not change the
header.

Specification: docs/spec/cpp-mapping.md#files
See also: gocpp explain initialization, gocpp explain linemap
Also known as: layout, output

Example (files.gp):

    package main

    import "fmt"

    var greeting = "hello"

    func main() {
    	fmt.Println(greeting)
    }

The C++ that gocpp emit -annotate writes for it:

    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #pragma once
    #include <gocpp/rt.hpp>

    namespace gpkg_main {
    void main();

    extern gp::string greeting;

    } // namespace gpkg_main
    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/files.gp.cpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/files.gp.cpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #include "gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp"

    namespace gpkg_main {

    // ---- ./files.gp:7: func main() {
    void main() {

    // ---- ./files.gp:8: fmt.Println(greeting)
    // gp[interfaces] col 2: fmt.Println: the runtime's gp::fmt functions take each operand with the
    //     descriptor of its Go type (gp::fmt::as), not boxed into an interface first (an operand of a
    //     non-pointer type with an Error method is, see the allocation note)
        gp::fmt::Println(greeting);

    // ---- ./files.gp:9: }
    }

    } // namespace gpkg_main
